# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# Item 5 of the HIG adoption: a destructive verb never rides Return.
# Empty Trash asks and its default is Cancel; Delete's question completes
# reversibly by default -- Return lands on Move to Trash, never Delete.
wait 12
note Empty Trash asks, and Return means Cancel: the load stays
click-desk .Trash 3
wait 4
menu-pick Empty Trash
wait 5
expect-alert empty the Trash
key Return
wait 5
expect-file /tmp/trk_home/.Trash/planted.txt
note an aimed answer empties it
click-desk .Trash 3
wait 4
menu-pick Empty Trash
wait 5
key e
wait 25
expect-no-file /tmp/trk_home/.Trash/planted.txt
note Delete asks; Return takes the reversible way through
click-row 1
wait 3
expect-selected-name a.txt
key Delete
wait 5
expect-alert cannot be reverted
key Return
wait 25
expect-file /tmp/trk_home/.Trash/a.txt
expect-no-file /tmp/trk_script/a.txt
quit
